<<
/Title (We live in a world shaped by data. From the recommendations on your streaming service, to the graphs in your lecture slides, to the fitness stats on your phone -data is embedded in nearly every part of modern life. Yet for many university students, it can feel intimidating or abstract. Data literacy, the ability to read, interpret and communicate data, is one of the most transferable skills you can develop at university, and one that employers across every industry are actively looking for. This handbook offers a practical starting point.)
